[
    {
        "content": "<p>I am trying to understand a wonderful blog for understanding grind tactic : <a href=\"https://www.philipzucker.com/lean_smt/\">https://www.philipzucker.com/lean_smt/</a></p>\n<p>And I am kinda confused as to how running the following command</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Bash\"><pre><span></span><code>!<span class=\"w\"> </span>lean<span class=\"w\"> </span>/tmp/test.lean<span class=\"w\"> </span>--json\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>for the file containing the following lean code</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">%%</span><span class=\"n\">file</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">tmp</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">test</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mytheorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mytheorem</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>leads to generating this info</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Bash\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"s2\">\"severity\"</span>:<span class=\"s2\">\"information\"</span>,<span class=\"s2\">\"pos\"</span>:<span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"s2\">\"line\"</span>:3,<span class=\"s2\">\"column\"</span>:0<span class=\"o\">}</span>,<span class=\"s2\">\"kind\"</span>:<span class=\"s2\">\"[anonymous]\"</span>,<span class=\"s2\">\"keepFullRange\"</span>:false,<span class=\"s2\">\"isSilent\"</span>:false,<span class=\"s2\">\"fileName\"</span>:<span class=\"s2\">\"/tmp/test.lean\"</span>,<span class=\"s2\">\"endPos\"</span>:<span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"s2\">\"line\"</span>:3,<span class=\"s2\">\"column\"</span>:6<span class=\"o\">}</span>,<span class=\"s2\">\"data\"</span>:<span class=\"s2\">\"mytheorem (p q : Prop) : p ∧ q → p\"</span>,<span class=\"s2\">\"caption\"</span>:<span class=\"s2\">\"\"</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>when I try to run the example (I am using the template generated by <code>lake init</code>) using <code>lean Main.lean --json</code></p>\n<p>I get the json with an error (the project name is Leanhack)</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">✗</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Main</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">--json</span>\n<span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"s2\">\"caption\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"s2\">\"\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"s2\">\"data\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"s2\">\"unknown module prefix 'Leanhack'</span><span class=\"se\">\\n\\n</span><span class=\"s2\">No directory 'Leanhack' or file 'Leanhack.olean' in the search path entries:</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s2\">/var/home/sk/.elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4-nightly---nightly-2026-04-13/lib/lean\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"s2\">\"endPos\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">null</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"s2\">\"fileName\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"s2\">\"Main.lean\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"s2\">\"isSilent\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"s2\">\"keepFullRange\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"s2\">\"kind\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"s2\">\"[anonymous]\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"s2\">\"pos\"</span><span class=\"o\">:{</span><span class=\"s2\">\"column\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"s2\">\"line\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">},</span><span class=\"s2\">\"severity\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"s2\">\"error\"</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The error is pretty much clear, it needs a .olean file. From the <code>lake help build</code> adding a -o flag at the end of <code>lake build Main.lean:leanArts</code> builds the .olean files as stated below.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Bash\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">  </span>leanArts<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span>default<span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\">    </span>Lean<span class=\"w\"> </span>artifacts<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span>*.olean,<span class=\"w\"> </span>*.ilean,<span class=\"w\"> </span>*.c<span class=\"w\"> </span>files<span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and the IR directory contains no .olean files</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Bash\"><pre><span></span><code>➜<span class=\"w\">  </span>ls<span class=\"w\"> </span>./.lake/build/ir/\nLeanhack<span class=\"w\">    </span>Leanhack.c.hash<span class=\"w\">      </span>Leanhack.c.o.export.hash<span class=\"w\">   </span>Leanhack.setup.json<span class=\"w\">  </span>Main.c.hash<span class=\"w\">      </span>Main.c.o.export.hash<span class=\"w\">   </span>Main.setup.json\nLeanhack.c<span class=\"w\">  </span>Leanhack.c.o.export<span class=\"w\">  </span>Leanhack.c.o.export.trace<span class=\"w\">  </span>Main.c<span class=\"w\">               </span>Main.c.o.export<span class=\"w\">  </span>Main.c.o.export.trace\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Essentially the problem - I am unable to generate a valid json as mentioned in the blog, how do I that?</p>",
        "id": 590304011,
        "sender_full_name": "Shubham Kumar 🦀 (he/him)",
        "timestamp": 1776892243
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If you want to run <code>lean</code> on a file importing other modules, the easiest way is to do</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">lake</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">file</span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"c1\">-- &lt;args&gt;...]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>If you run</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">lake</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Main</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lean</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>you get the actual command being run.</p>\n<p>For your example you can do</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">lake</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Main</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- --json</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Note that only the messages from the module being compiled are written to JSON output. That is, when the messages are created in a module you are importing then they are not written to that JSON.</p>",
        "id": 590469319,
        "sender_full_name": "fiforeach",
        "timestamp": 1776950372
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>ok so I was able to get the output using <code>lake lean Main.lean -- --json</code></p>\n<p>Thank you &lt;3</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">✗</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">lake</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Main</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- --json</span>\n<span class=\"n\">note</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">toolchain</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">'</span><span class=\"n\">leanprover</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">lean4</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">nightly</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">nightly</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">2026</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">04</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">13</span><span class=\"bp\">'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">override</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">on</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">'/</span><span class=\"n\">var</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">home</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">sk</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">leanhack'</span>\n<span class=\"n\">note</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">remove</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">elan</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">override</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">unset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">--path '/var/home/sk/leanhack' | to suppress: ELAN_NO_OVERRIDE_NOTICE=1</span>\n<span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"s2\">\"caption\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"s2\">\"\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"s2\">\"data\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"s2\">\"`grind` failed</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s2\">case grind</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s2\">p q : Prop</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s2\">h : p ∨ q</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s2\">h_1 : ¬p</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s2\">⊢ False</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s2\">[grind] Goal diagnostics</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s2\">  [facts] Asserted facts</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s2\">    [prop] p ∨ q</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s2\">    [prop] ¬p</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s2\">  [eqc] True propositions</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s2\">    [prop] q</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s2\">    [prop] p ∨ q</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s2\">  [eqc] False propositions</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s2\">    [prop] p\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"s2\">\"endPos\"</span><span class=\"o\">:{</span><span class=\"s2\">\"column\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">56</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"s2\">\"line\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">},</span><span class=\"s2\">\"fileName\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"s2\">\"/var/home/sk/leanhack/Main.lean\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"s2\">\"isSilent\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"s2\">\"keepFullRange\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"s2\">\"kind\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"s2\">\"[anonymous]\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"s2\">\"pos\"</span><span class=\"o\">:{</span><span class=\"s2\">\"column\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">51</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"s2\">\"line\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">},</span><span class=\"s2\">\"severity\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"s2\">\"error\"</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"s2\">\"caption\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"s2\">\"\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"s2\">\"data\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"s2\">\"mytheorem (p q : Prop) : p ∨ q → p\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"s2\">\"endPos\"</span><span class=\"o\">:{</span><span class=\"s2\">\"column\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">6</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"s2\">\"line\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"o\">},</span><span class=\"s2\">\"fileName\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"s2\">\"/var/home/sk/leanhack/Main.lean\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"s2\">\"isSilent\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"s2\">\"keepFullRange\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"s2\">\"kind\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"s2\">\"[anonymous]\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"s2\">\"pos\"</span><span class=\"o\">:{</span><span class=\"s2\">\"column\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"s2\">\"line\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"o\">},</span><span class=\"s2\">\"severity\"</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"s2\">\"information\"</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
